## Candor Intake Gateway (C-05) - tor instance `candor-intake`.
## Managed file, do not edit. Installed as /etc/tor/instances/candor-intake/torrc,
## root:root 0644. The self-test compares its hash with the release manifest
## (16-TOR-I2P.md NET-004, 32-OPERATIONS.md `tor.config_hash`); any local change is a FAIL.
## Template: 16-TOR-I2P.md §7.1. Deviations from §7.1 are listed in deploy/SPEC-NOTES.md
## (all of them are stricter, none weakens a §7.1 setting).
## Only tunables documented in 16 §7.1 notes (PoW / intro-DoS numbers) may differ per site.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Process / host
## systemd runs tor in the foreground as _tor-candor-intake (16 §7.3, unit tor@candor-intake).
RunAsDaemon 0
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor-instances/candor-intake
## NET-010: seccomp sandbox; no debugger attach; no core dumps (LimitCORE=0 in the unit).
Sandbox 1
DisableDebuggerAttachment 1
AvoidDiskWrites 1
HardwareAccel 1
## NET-010 / 16 §7.3: the unit sets MemoryDenyWriteExecute=yes, so the Equi-X/HashX JIT
## must not be used; the interpreted PoW verifier is used instead (deploy/SPEC-NOTES.md D-03).
CompiledProofOfWorkHash 0

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Not a client proxy, relay, bridge or exit
## NET-011, 16 §7.4 lint. NET-045: the source onion instance has no SocksPort.
## No clearnet listener of any kind (NET-002, ADR-002, 16 §14).
SocksPort 0
TransPort 0
NATDPort 0
DNSPort 0
HTTPTunnelPort 0
ORPort 0
DirPort 0
ExitRelay 0
ExitPolicy reject *:*
BridgeRelay 0
PublishServerDescriptor 0

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Control interface
## NET-009: no TCP ControlPort; Unix socket only with cookie auth; group _candor-torctl
## (health exporter only - the vanguards add-on is not deployed, ADR-049(1)).
ControlPort 0
ControlSocket /run/tor-instances/candor-intake/control.sock
ControlSocketsGroupWritable 1
CookieAuthentication 1
CookieAuthFile /run/tor-instances/candor-intake/control.authcookie
CookieAuthFileGroupReadable 1

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Logging: minimal, no client/circuit data
## NET-008 / LOG-005 / 32 `tor.log_level`: level warn, never a file. stderr is captured
## by journald in the volatile `candor-intake` namespace (journald@candor-intake.conf,
## Storage=volatile, <= 24 h). LOG-005 asks for stderr; 16 §7.1 says syslog - stderr is
## used so that no syslog daemon can ever receive tor output (SPEC-NOTES D-02).
Log warn stderr
SafeLogging 1
LogMessageDomains 0
## LOG-005: coarse log timestamps (1 h) so that no tor message carries a precise time.
LogTimeGranularity 1 hour
## LOG-005: no onion-service statistics.
HiddenServiceStatistics 0

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Guard / padding defaults kept explicit
## ADR-001 as amended by ADR-049(1): vanguards-lite on every profile (incl. HIGH);
## the Python vanguards add-on SHALL NOT be deployed (NET-007).
UseEntryGuards 1
VanguardsLiteEnabled 1
ConnectionPadding 1
ReducedConnectionPadding 0
CircuitPadding 1
ReducedCircuitPadding 0

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Onion service: source intake
## NET-001 (Tor v3 onion only), NET-019 / NET-043 / ADR-028 / ADR-032 (key only here,
## HiddenServiceDir 0700, key 0600, on the LUKS volume; see secret-placement.toml).
HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor-instances/candor-intake/hs-source/
HiddenServiceVersion 3
## NET-002: target is a Unix socket only (socket unit candor-intake-web.socket, 0660
## candor-web:_tor-candor-intake). Exactly one HiddenServicePort (16 §7.4).
## Onion-TLS mode (NET-042) REPLACES this line with port 443 -> https.sock.
HiddenServicePort 80 unix:/run/candor/source-web/http.sock
HiddenServiceAllowUnknownPorts 0
HiddenServiceDirGroupReadable 0
HiddenServiceNumIntroductionPoints 5
HiddenServiceMaxStreams 32
HiddenServiceMaxStreamsCloseCircuit 1
## 16 §7.1 / §13 L4: per-circuit identifier for in-memory rate limiting in C-06 only
## (NET-013: never persisted or logged). 17 §5.5 says "no ExportCircuitID" - conflict
## recorded in SPEC-NOTES D-04; 16 §7.1 (NET-004) is followed.
HiddenServiceExportCircuitID haproxy
## NET-005: single-hop / non-anonymous modes are forbidden.
HiddenServiceSingleHopMode 0
HiddenServiceNonAnonymousMode 0

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- DoS defences (ADR-026, NET-006, 16 §13)
## Numeric values are site tunables within the bounds of 34; defaults per 16 §7.1.
HiddenServicePoWDefensesEnabled 1
HiddenServicePoWQueueRate 250
HiddenServicePoWQueueBurst 2500
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSDefense 1
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSRatePerSec 25
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSBurstPerSec 200
